# PARK GUELL (2026-11-02, REBUILT ON ITS PLAN 2026-11-04): Gaudi's garden city on the Muntanya Pelada, Barcelona, 1900-1914
# -- its monumental core and the hillside round it, as one landmark. Writes assets/architecture/park-guell.json and
# assets/finishes/park-guell.json; the pieces are gaudi.py's components (pavilion, mushroom, hyperboloid tower, cross) and
# helpers (bench profile, leaning portico, hypostyle), the curves `sweep`s, the hill a `terrain` (arch/assemble.js).
#
# THE FRAME: metres, origin the main gate on Carrer d'Olot (OSM node 402883145, 41.413488 N 2.1530954 E), y up from the
# gate's ground (131.0 m above sea level), +z down the park's axis to the street (bearing 138.3, SE: the line from the prow
# of the Nature Square to the gate), +x along the street to the north-east (the porter's lodge's side). The axis of the
# stair, the dragon and the hall is x = -0.5 (AX).
#
# SOURCED -- OpenStreetMap (api 0.6 map call, 2026-11-04; converted to the frame, to 0.1 m):
#   the square: way 1105836977 (2701 m2; sources give 2694), its prow at z -42.8, its back at z -126;
#   the serpentine bench: ways 1105836969 + 1105836965 + 1105836970, traced along its outer face; the hypostyle room:
#   relation 14718228 (the bench's line and way 1105836971 across its back) -- a pentagon of 1503 m2 (sources: 1500 m2),
#   42 m wide, 43.7 m deep (sources: 43 m); the stair: the eight flights 451140325/30/28/24 (west) and 451140333/23/31/29
#   (east), 11, 11, 11, 12 steps, from z -17.6 to z -41; the dragon: way 295826465 at z -33.6 on the axis; the porter's
#   lodge (Casa del Guarda, way 672895475) right of the gate (x 4.2..19.9), the administration pavilion (way 672895651,
#   now the shop) left (x -18.2..-4.9), the gate between them 9.1 m; the coach house: way 672895744; the boundary wall
#   along the street: ways 1430523773 and 1430523772; the washerwoman's portico: the retaining wall 460419313 it is built
#   against (85 m of it, from its bend to its east end; sources: 83 m) and node 4790341321; the three viaducts: ways
#   61942877 (de Baix), 61942853 (del Mig), 629678545 (de Dalt); the Casa-Museu Gaudi: way 126856515; the Casa Larrard
#   (the school): way 672896040.
# SOURCED -- the ground: the IGN's MDT05 (5 m digital terrain model, servicios.idee.es WCS, coverage Elevacion4258_5),
#   sampled on the frame's 5 m grid: the square a flat terrace at +17.9 (17.0-18.3 sampled), the vestibule +0..+1.0, the
#   stair's head about +8.5, the street rising 11 m to the west, the hill behind to +50 and more.
# SOURCED -- es/ca.wikipedia, parkguell.barcelona: the wall 2-4 m high, 15 medallions 1.4 m across; the porter's lodge
#   14.80 x 7.66 m, 21 m high; the administration pavilion 12.60 x 6.60 m, 29 m high, its cross 3.8 m; the stair 45
#   steps, its side walls, three fountains (the grotto, the arms with the snake, the dragon 2.4 m long) and the odeon's
#   bench on the last landing; the hall: 86 Doric columns 6.16 m tall, 1.20 m across, trencadis to 1.8 m, the outer ones
#   inclined, 90 planned and 4 left out for Jujol's rosettes 3 m across, 14 medallions; the viaducts: the lower one's two
#   files of leaning columns, the upper two's three files.
# MEASURED from Commons photographs (the stair from its foot; the hall 1909): the hall's grid is square and set along
#   the axis -- two front columns flank the stair's head, the axis column stands a bay behind them; the cornice and
#   the bench above it wave with the bench's loops.
# ESTIMATED (flagged): the grid's step (3.8 m: the step at which 90 places fall inside the pentagon with the front pair
#   and the axis column where the photograph has them); the rosettes' places; the hall's floor (+8.6: 45 risers of
#   16.9 cm from the vestibule's +1.0, the DTM's +8..+9.9 at the stair's head); the vaults' rise and the slab; the
#   outer columns' lean (5 deg); which end of the administration pavilion carries the cross tower (the gate's); the
#   pavilions' storeys, roofs and towers within the sourced totals (as in 2026-11-02); the viaducts' decks (straight
#   between the heights where their ends meet the ground) and their galleries' heights; the porticoes' sections; the
#   Casa-Museu's and the Casa Larrard's heights; the trees (crowns found in the World Imagery tiles, 8.5 m apart at most;
#   their kinds by place -- palms about the square, carobs low, pines high -- and the glades a slow field, not sourced).
# ADDED 2026-11-05 (round-2 review): the paths -- every OSM footway/steps/path/track inside the park's outline (way
#   66713401) clear of what is built, cut into the hill; the Calvary on the Turo de les Tres Creus (OSM peak 6286148116,
#   185 m, at x -201 z -19: the height map now runs from x -290) -- its round mound and two flights estimated, the crosses
#   1.7 and 1.5 m (es.wikipedia), the tallest the four-armed one; El Drac re-carved as a salamander on a bed of stone.
